rdma-core v61.0: honour sq_sig_all in providers/ionic

libfabric's verbs provider never sets IBV_SEND_SIGNALED -- its send flags
are only ever inline-or-nothing -- and gets its completions by creating
every queue pair with sq_sig_all = 1, meaning "complete every send
whatever the work request says".

v61.0's ionic provider passes sq_sig_all through to create_qp_ex and then
never stores or consults it. The only thing that marks a send as
completing is the per-request IBV_SEND_SIGNALED flag, and ionic_poll_send
discards anything not so marked. So a queue pair created with
sq_sig_all = 1 yields no successful send completions at all: the device
completes the send, the provider swallows it.

Under libfabric that shows up as a hard cutoff at the inject limit.
Payloads of 255 bytes or less go through fi_inject, which needs no
transmit buffer and no completion, and work indefinitely. At 256 bytes
rxm_emulate_inject takes a buffer from the tx pool that can only be
returned when the completion arrives -- which it never does -- and every
subsequent send returns -FI_EAGAIN forever, with nothing logging it.

This is not specific to the emulated device; any libfabric-over-ionic
deployment hits it. Fixed upstream after v61.0 (present at
bd3282a1cf1025c7869a8664c2d54266a4dded44); this is that change backported
to the v61.0 the guests' libibverbs ABI requires, since building the
upstream tree produces a provider for ABI rdmav65 that libibverbs 61.0
will not load.

--- a/providers/ionic/ionic.h
+++ b/providers/ionic/ionic.h
@@ -193,6 +193,7 @@ struct ionic_qp {
 	bool			has_sq;
 	bool			has_rq;
 	bool			lockfree;
+	bool			sig_all;

 	struct list_node	cq_poll_sq;
 	struct list_node	cq_poll_rq;
--- a/providers/ionic/ionic_verbs.c
+++ b/providers/ionic/ionic_verbs.c
@@ -1692,6 +1692,7 @@ static struct ibv_qp *ionic_create_qp_ex(struct ibv_context *ibctx,
 	qp->has_sq = true;
 	qp->has_rq = true;
 	qp->lockfree = false;
+	qp->sig_all = ex->sq_sig_all;

 	list_node_init(&qp->cq_poll_sq);
 	list_node_init(&qp->cq_poll_rq);
@@ -2113,7 +2114,7 @@ static void ionic_v1_prep_base(struct ionic_qp *qp,
 	if (wr->send_flags & IBV_SEND_SOLICITED)
 		wqe->base.flags |= htobe16(IONIC_V1_FLAG_SOL);

-	if (wr->send_flags & IBV_SEND_SIGNALED) {
+	if (qp->sig_all || (wr->send_flags & IBV_SEND_SIGNALED)) {
 		wqe->base.flags |= htobe16(IONIC_V1_FLAG_SIG);
 		meta->signal = true;
 	}
